1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,785
Agents reuse prior work.

2
00:00:01,785 --> 00:00:06,694
When an input changes, which saved numbers can they still trust?

3
00:00:06,694 --> 00:00:10,468
ProofFlow keeps the dependencies attached across runs.

4
00:00:10,468 --> 00:00:12,778
Correct the euro exchange rate.

5
00:00:12,778 --> 00:00:15,551
Revenue becomes stale and is withheld.

6
00:00:15,551 --> 00:00:21,746
The independent support count stays current, while previous revenue remains clearly historical.

7
00:00:21,746 --> 00:00:29,274
HydraDB traces the inputs each tool actually consumed, linking this calculation to both reports.

8
00:00:29,274 --> 00:00:32,272
Four tools refresh the dependent work.

9
00:00:32,272 --> 00:00:36,770
Company revenue becomes five thousand seven hundred fifty-five dollars;

10
00:00:36,770 --> 00:00:40,767
EU revenue, two thousand two hundred eighty.

11
00:00:40,767 --> 00:00:42,916
Independent recomputation matches.

12
00:00:42,916 --> 00:00:47,535
Now a separate retail experiment: six hundred forty public

13
00:00:47,535 --> 00:00:52,155
transaction lines, four dated partitions, and ten authored cases.

14
00:00:52,155 --> 00:00:58,450
Complete dependencies refresh 38 recoverable reports and block four unavailable ones.

15
00:00:58,450 --> 00:01:03,490
With identical records and the graph's per-case allowance, BM25

16
00:01:03,490 --> 00:01:07,156
completes nineteen, dense eight, and iterative hybrid thirty-three.

17
00:01:07,156 --> 00:01:10,555
All methods share the same executor.

18
00:01:10,555 --> 00:01:16,626
Evidence uses 69.41% fewer tokens than full context.

19
00:01:16,626 --> 00:01:18,650
Exact dependency traversal ties.

20
00:01:18,650 --> 00:01:21,324
The calculations still run.

21
00:01:21,324 --> 00:01:26,747
At a fixed 2,048-token limit, graph completes only eight reports.

22
00:01:26,747 --> 00:01:30,002
The earlier development efficiency gate failed.

23
00:01:30,002 --> 00:01:32,821
Both limitations remain visible.

24
00:01:32,821 --> 00:01:37,376
An actual Claude client uses five MCP tools

25
00:01:37,376 --> 00:01:41,020
to load data, choose plans, inspect and refresh.

26
00:01:41,020 --> 00:01:44,664
It reuses prior artifacts on authored two-row input.

27
00:01:44,664 --> 00:01:48,764
After a launch-configuration fix, one trajectory passed 32 checks,

28
00:01:48,764 --> 00:01:52,408
with nine requests and twelve recorded runtime calls.

29
00:01:52,408 --> 00:01:55,791
Its first configuration failure is retained.

30
00:01:55,791 --> 00:02:00,000
ProofFlow: current evidence across agent runs.
